846
00:56:14,840 --> 00:56:17,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor, good evening.

847
00:56:18,600 --> 00:56:28,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Earlier this year, DBM issued Corporate Budget Memorandum No. 48 for the Fiscal Year 2027 Corporate Budget Call.

848
00:56:28,980 --> 00:56:31,000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Under the policy, it was stated that the DBM should not be involved in corporate budget calls.

849
00:56:31,020 --> 00:56:51,100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Under the policy, it was stated that a GOCC receiving 60% or more its funding from national government subsidies for the past 10 consecutive years is automatically flagged for mandatory institutional review for GOCCs covered by Republic Act No. 10149.

850
00:56:51,640 --> 00:56:58,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That review is to be conducted by GCG. Is this correct, Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor?

851
00:56:59,180 --> 00:57:00,000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

852
00:57:01,020 --> 00:57:15,080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And my follow-up question, then under those parameters, how many GOCCs under GCG's jurisdiction currently meet the 60% subsidy for 10 years threshold?

853
00:57:19,280 --> 00:57:22,380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The study is ongoing regarding the number, Mr. Speaker.

854
00:57:22,380 --> 00:57:26,380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Are we talking about 2026?

855
00:57:28,980 --> 00:57:30,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Or 2025, I mean? I'm sorry.

856
00:57:50,740 --> 00:57:55,758
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The GCG is just checking their records, Mr. Speaker.

857
00:58:01,462 --> 00:58:01,833
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ...

858
00:58:31,020 --> 00:58:44,380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The GCG will just submit the list of GOCCs that satisfy their requirement, Mr. Speaker.

859
00:58:44,520 --> 00:58:46,240
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: That's okay with my distinguished colleague.

860
00:58:47,460 --> 00:58:49,000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Fair enough, Mr. Speaker.

861
00:58:49,480 --> 00:58:50,720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I gladly accept that.

862
00:58:51,700 --> 00:58:53,160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: My next question,

863
00:58:55,680 --> 00:59:01,000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: have institutional reviews which are now mandated already commenced?

864
00:59:01,020 --> 00:59:03,240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: For every one of those GOCCs.

865
00:59:03,700 --> 00:59:07,140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: If not, what the timetables are we looking at?

866
00:59:31,020 --> 00:59:39,200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Regarding the monitoring and evaluation of GOCCs, Mr. Speaker, the GCG currently conducts three.

867
00:59:40,500 --> 00:59:41,400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, three.

868
00:59:42,040 --> 00:59:48,840
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: There's the performance evaluation system for GOCCs, and then there's the performance evaluation for directors in the GOCC sector.

869
00:59:49,440 --> 00:59:54,020
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And then the GCG also produces corporate governance scorecards.

870
00:59:54,020 --> 00:59:59,940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: But as per the finalization of the reports for fiscal year 2020,

871
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,580
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the GCG is dependent on the submission of COA financial statement.

872
01:00:07,220 --> 01:00:10,720
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So as of now, review is still currently ongoing, Mr. Speaker.

873
01:00:10,860 --> 01:00:15,480
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So do we expect that later this year or it's going to be next year?

874
01:00:16,300 --> 01:00:17,980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, later in this year, Mr. Speaker.

875
01:00:18,360 --> 01:00:21,320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How many directors are, as you mentioned, that under review?

876
01:00:22,240 --> 01:00:22,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How many of them?

877
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:54,000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: For, Mr. Speaker, for clarification, director, total directors for all the GOCCs that are being reviewed, total.

878
01:00:57,540 --> 01:00:59,820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: We're pulling up the actual number.

879
01:01:00,000 --> 01:01:03,880
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So estimated around, approximately around 500 directors, Mr. Speaker.

880
01:01:04,420 --> 01:01:06,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

881
01:01:10,240 --> 01:01:21,200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor, could the good sponsor provide the following information for the consideration of this body?

882
01:01:21,680 --> 01:01:29,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The amount of national government support received by these GOCCs during the past 10 years, its performance, scorecard results,

883
01:01:29,940 --> 01:01:34,100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and the current status of GCG's institutional review.

884
01:01:36,600 --> 01:01:46,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: It's important because the new DBM policy says they are now subject to mandatory institutional review to be conducted by GCG.

885
01:01:48,380 --> 01:01:52,080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kasi po, meron na pong DBM policy na bago ngayon.

886
01:01:53,080 --> 01:01:58,080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Mr. Speaker, just to clarify, the first would be the amount of government support received by the GOCCs.

887
01:01:58,080 --> 01:02:01,060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: What's the second one, Mr. Speaker?

888
01:02:02,440 --> 01:02:08,060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: No, that's the question because I'm just interjecting that there's a new DBM policy.

889
01:02:09,160 --> 01:02:16,520
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Now, they have to be subjected for mandatory institutional review to be conducted by GCG.

890
01:02:16,520 --> 01:02:21,720
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, sir. Government support.

891
01:02:21,720 --> 01:02:28,060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, sir. Government support.

892
01:02:38,220 --> 01:02:43,400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, the GCG is just pulling up the actual number.

893
01:02:43,540 --> 01:02:48,380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: However, just an overall observation regarding the amount of government support,

894
01:02:48,600 --> 01:02:56,940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it's been declining given that those GOCCs that previously needed government support are now improving in performance.

895
01:02:57,140 --> 01:02:58,040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you.

896
01:02:58,060 --> 01:02:58,700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

897
01:03:04,220 --> 01:03:11,220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: According to GCG's classification as of June 30, 2026,

898
01:03:11,940 --> 01:03:16,420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: there are 21 corporations classified under abolition,

899
01:03:17,880 --> 01:03:20,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: meaning they are being considered for closure,

900
01:03:22,180 --> 01:03:26,280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: winding down or absorption into other government corporations.

901
01:03:26,920 --> 01:03:38,460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: GCG was subsequently reported as saying that the Commission hopes to complete the liquidation of at least five of them within 2026.

902
01:03:39,300 --> 01:03:41,060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is that still the target?

903
01:03:43,640 --> 01:03:44,280
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

904
01:03:44,780 --> 01:03:46,420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Mr. Speaker, that is correct.

905
01:03:46,420 --> 01:03:55,480
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: As of June 30, there are 21 GOCCs that have been abolished and under liquidation.

906
01:03:55,900 --> 01:03:56,160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And there's also...

907
01:03:56,160 --> 01:03:58,700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And there's also 11 that has been abolished and completed liquidation.

908
01:03:59,380 --> 01:04:08,360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: As for the number of GOCCs with terminal reports to be submitted to the Office of the President,

909
01:04:08,540 --> 01:04:10,200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: there are 11 for this year.

910
01:04:10,800 --> 01:04:11,220
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker.

911
01:04:11,480 --> 01:04:11,620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah.

912
01:04:13,080 --> 01:04:14,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, this is your sponsor.

913
01:04:15,680 --> 01:04:17,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Without prejudice to the non-disclosure,

914
01:04:18,920 --> 01:04:23,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: may din nyo bangbanggitin kung sino mo ito or it's going under review pa rin?

915
01:04:23,020 --> 01:04:26,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Or if not, you can submit to this...

916
01:04:26,160 --> 01:04:29,600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: to this body kung sino yung mga yon.

917
01:04:30,140 --> 01:04:38,780
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: If you think it's going to be a violation of any rules or guidelines under GCG.

918
01:04:43,920 --> 01:04:45,160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Oh, sorry.

919
01:04:45,240 --> 01:04:46,540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: I stand corrected, Mr. Speaker.

920
01:04:46,840 --> 01:04:53,160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The number of abolished GOCCs pipeline for terminal report in 2026 is actually five.

921
01:04:54,380 --> 01:04:54,500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yeah.

922
01:04:54,500 --> 01:04:55,080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: But...

923
01:04:55,080 --> 01:04:55,780
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: But...

924
01:04:55,780 --> 01:04:59,340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That's why I was mentioned a while ago that there are still five.

925
01:04:59,740 --> 01:05:02,240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That's why for my next question,

926
01:05:03,300 --> 01:05:07,240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: that means even five are completed this year.

927
01:05:07,240 --> 01:05:11,640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: A significant number will still remain under abolition status.

928
01:05:12,140 --> 01:05:17,360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: For how long has each of these 21 corporations been under abolition?

929
01:05:48,440 --> 01:05:57,800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Um, Mr. Speaker, given the extensive process of settling the obligations and liabilities of those GOCCs

930
01:05:58,440 --> 01:06:20,860
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Those GOCCs that are non-performing, as well as the fulfillment of compromise agreements, it's a lengthy period. As early as 2013, there are still GOCCs that are being processed. So, roughly around 13 years.

931
01:06:21,460 --> 01:06:28,420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah, Mr. Speaker. For the information of everyone, GOCC stands for government-owned controlled corporation.

932
01:06:28,440 --> 01:06:46,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Am I right? And they're not asking subsidy or funding from our government, only GCG. Now, because my understanding, when you're a GOCC, you generate income. Am I right?

933
01:06:47,640 --> 01:06:48,060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

934
01:06:48,060 --> 01:06:49,860
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

935
01:06:49,960 --> 01:06:58,260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, how come those 5 or 21 you mentioned, Wilco, are winding down or for abolition? Ibig ho bang sabihin?

936
01:06:59,020 --> 01:07:03,880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Nalulugi, hindi sila kumikita, or part of downsizing talaga?

937
01:07:05,680 --> 01:07:18,920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, based on the charter of the GCG and all of its guidelines, there are six qualifications for the recommendation of this positive action.

938
01:07:20,120 --> 01:07:26,960
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: One, the GOCC's function is no longer relevant to state or national development policy.

939
01:07:27,520 --> 01:07:28,400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Second, it...

940
01:07:28,440 --> 01:07:33,300
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It's duplicate or unnecessarily overlaps with other government agencies.

941
01:07:33,300 --> 01:07:40,240
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The third one, the GOCC is not producing desired outcomes or is no longer achieving its objectives, as stated.

942
01:07:40,980 --> 01:07:45,500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The fourth would be, the GOCC would be dormant or non-operational.

943
01:07:46,420 --> 01:07:57,300
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The fifth would be, the GOCC would be involved in activities that is determined to be best carried out by a private sector firm.

944
01:07:58,440 --> 01:08:04,960
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And the sixth one would be, the GOCC's nature of operations would require consolidation under a holding company.

945
01:08:05,480 --> 01:08:09,420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, those are the six qualifications for recommendation for abolition, Mr. Speaker.

946
01:08:09,420 --> 01:08:16,240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The number five, or I think number five, you mentioned number four, that is going to be sold to private.

947
01:08:16,820 --> 01:08:18,200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is that what I understand?

948
01:08:18,460 --> 01:08:19,580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Tama ba yun? Intindi ko?

949
01:08:20,300 --> 01:08:21,420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Uh, there...

950
01:08:23,060 --> 01:08:26,540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Okay.

951
01:08:26,540 --> 01:08:26,620
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Okay.

952
01:08:28,440 --> 01:08:47,920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The fifth one, Mr. Speaker, the GCG assesses and sees if the activity in which the GOCC is involved would be best carried out by a private sector firm.

953
01:08:48,820 --> 01:08:54,260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, when you say best carried out by a private firm, what does it mean?

954
01:08:54,260 --> 01:08:57,140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Are we going to sell it or just going to give it away?

955
01:08:57,660 --> 01:08:58,260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Anong bang...

956
01:08:58,440 --> 01:09:03,840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ang tindi sa private firm will just be carried away.

957
01:09:04,260 --> 01:09:05,220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: It will be carried out.

958
01:09:17,520 --> 01:09:18,000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Okay.

959
01:09:29,520 --> 01:09:37,770
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: [unclear]

960
01:09:38,430 --> 01:09:39,550
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: [unclear]

961
01:09:50,650 --> 01:09:52,240
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: [unclear]

962
01:10:07,690 --> 01:10:11,400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, regarding abolition,

963
01:10:11,400 --> 01:10:12,360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: if the

964
01:10:12,360 --> 01:10:14,360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: particular GOCC would be

965
01:10:14,360 --> 01:10:15,760
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: recommended for abolition,

966
01:10:17,180 --> 01:10:18,000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it's usually

967
01:10:18,000 --> 01:10:19,460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the

968
01:10:19,460 --> 01:10:22,180
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: employees, the assets,

969
01:10:22,180 --> 01:10:23,940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and all the operations would be

970
01:10:23,940 --> 01:10:26,080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: absorbed by the government

971
01:10:26,080 --> 01:10:27,940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: agency, like a relevant government

972
01:10:27,940 --> 01:10:29,980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: agency, with related

973
01:10:29,980 --> 01:10:32,340
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: operations to the GOCC for abolition.

974
01:10:32,700 --> 01:10:33,080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker.

975
01:10:33,620 --> 01:10:35,340
