01:35:04,100 --> 01:35:30,000
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Sponsor. In fact, merong mga tumaas pagdating sa allowances, benefits, and incentives; merong mga nabigyan kasi before wala yung iba. In-standardize sa CPCS 1, CPCS 2, pero ang daming problematic provisions at may pushback yung workers in GFIs.

1384
01:35:30,000 --> 01:35:59,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: In fact, Madam Sponsor, bago pa man nagkaroon ng batas na bumuo sa GCG at bago CPCS 1 and CPCS 2, may mga manggagawa sa GFIs na nag-e-enjoy na ng iba?t ibang allowances, benefits, and incentives.

1385
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:29,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: For example, Pag-IBIG educational assistance and provident fund traced to board resolutions from 1986 and 1994. PDIC has 2011 payroll records, the year RA 10149 was passed, showing 14th-month pay and provident fund contributions. SSS PRAISE program disbursing

1386
01:36:30,000 --> 01:36:59,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: 434.805 million in incentives in 2024 was reviewed and approved by the Civil Service Commission in June 2024. Dahil sa CPCS 1 and CPCS 2, may mga benepisyong nawala o nabawasan sa mga manggagawa sa GFIs.

1387
01:37:00,000 --> 01:37:29,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Sa provident fund, some were enjoying 40% employer share, pero dahil sa CPCS 1 and CPCS 2, 10% na lang. Iyan ang malaking problema. Madam Sponsor, let us establish a basic principle of law.

1388
01:37:30,000 --> 01:37:59,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang Republic Act 10149, GOCC Governance Act, ay pinasa noong 2011, a general law for standardization of GOCCs. Fast forward to 2019, ipinasa ng Kongreso ang RA 11199, Social Security Act of 2018, isang specific law.

1389
01:38:00,000 --> 01:38:29,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Section 3(d) gave the Social Security Commission power to fix reasonable compensation, allowances, and benefits of its personnel. Ngayon ginagamit ng GCG yung CPCS 2 na inilabas noong 2025

1390
01:38:30,000 --> 01:38:59,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: para i-override at tanggalin ang mga benepisyong ito. In constant communication ako sa union ng SSS. So alin ang mas mataas, Madam Sponsor, isang batas na pinasa ng Kongreso o isang executive order

1391
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:01,970
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: na nanggaling sa Office of the President, Madam Sponsor, Mr. Speaker?

1392
01:39:03,790 --> 01:39:06,810
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: [unclear]

1393
01:39:30,000 --> 01:39:33,360
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Mr. Speaker, yung time ko po pumapatak.

1394
01:39:39,560 --> 01:39:40,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pumapatak po yung time ko.

1395
01:39:41,500 --> 01:39:42,300
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Timer, please.

1396
01:40:57,780 --> 01:40:58,160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: [unclear]

1397
01:41:02,760 --> 01:41:29,610
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: [unclear]

1398
01:41:30,510 --> 01:41:36,420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, Section 11 of RA 10149, if I may read,

1399
01:41:37,060 --> 01:41:41,400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the Compensation and Position Classification System, so CPCS,

1400
01:41:42,860 --> 01:41:46,080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: to be developed and recommended by the GCG as approved by the President

1401
01:41:46,080 --> 01:41:49,780
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: shall apply to all positions on full or part-time basis now existing

1402
01:41:49,780 --> 01:41:52,040
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: or hereafter created in the GOCC,

1403
01:41:52,600 --> 01:41:57,480
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: provided that in no case shall there be any diminution in the authorized salaries

1404
01:41:57,480 --> 01:41:59,340
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: as of December 31, 2010.

1405
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:07,400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Of incumbent employees of the GOCCs, including those exempt under RA 6758 as amended

1406
01:42:07,400 --> 01:42:10,980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: upon the implementation of the CPCS for GOCCs.

1407
01:42:10,980 --> 01:42:14,520
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, dapat ang nagpe-prevail po talaga ay ano?

1408
01:42:15,260 --> 01:42:16,820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 10149, Mr. Speaker.

1409
01:42:17,380 --> 01:42:19,600
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ay, dapat ang nagpe-prevail ay yung?

1410
01:42:20,200 --> 01:42:21,760
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 10149, Mr. Speaker.

1411
01:42:21,780 --> 01:42:29,900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, in statutory construction, the specific and later law prevails over a general and earlier law.

1412
01:42:30,000 --> 01:42:39,120
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, given that RA 11199, 2019, is both the later law and the specific charter for SSS,

1413
01:42:39,840 --> 01:42:45,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: hindi po dapat ito ang mas masunod kaysa sa general framework ng RA 10149?

1414
01:42:51,520 --> 01:42:55,920
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Actually, ang basis yung executive order eh.

1415
01:42:56,840 --> 01:42:58,620
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, ano pong authority?

1416
01:43:00,000 --> 01:43:06,060
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang ginagamit ng GCG to use an executive order

1417
01:43:06,060 --> 01:43:13,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: to execute an implied administrative repeal of a specific act of Congress.

1418
01:43:15,080 --> 01:43:19,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ibig sabihin po ba nito, mas mataas na ang GCG kaysa sa Kongreso?

1419
01:43:21,720 --> 01:43:23,140
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kasi yun po ang efekte.

1420
01:43:36,680 --> 01:43:48,560
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, there was no express repeal of this section under the Social Security Law. So this would still prevail.

1421
01:43:48,560 --> 01:43:58,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, tinitindigan po ng GCG na through the executive order, eh pinangingibabawan niya.

1422
01:43:58,880 --> 01:43:59,320
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Halimbawa, yun dito sa...

1423
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:06,040
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Sabi dun sa case ng SSS, na batas na ginawa,

1424
01:44:07,380 --> 01:44:15,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: binigyan ng kapangyarihan ang SSS na i-determine yung compensation for the workers, for its workers.

1425
01:44:16,500 --> 01:44:21,320
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: And now, GCG is saying, hindi, mas mataas itong RA 10149.

1426
01:44:22,240 --> 01:44:27,240
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, paano ngayon natin i-reconcile yun, Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor?

1427
01:44:30,000 --> 01:44:31,780
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Oh, yeah.

1428
01:44:33,020 --> 01:44:36,300
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Given that there is no, but as for the GCG,

1429
01:44:36,420 --> 01:44:44,640
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: given that there is no express repeal of RA 10149 under the Social Security Law,

1430
01:44:44,760 --> 01:44:45,780
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it would still prevail.

1431
01:44:45,960 --> 01:44:51,700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Though, again, the GCG would submit to the wisdom of Congress if we need to amend.

1432
01:44:52,240 --> 01:44:58,500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Because under Section 11, nakaprovide po dito yung, as approved by the President.

1433
01:44:59,340 --> 01:44:59,500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So...

1434
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:13,340
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, big sabihin, si GCG magre-rely ngayon sa sabihin ng Presidente, even though the law is very clear.

1435
01:45:14,260 --> 01:45:19,440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Sponsor, Mr. Speaker, yan po yung kinagagalitan ng mga manggagawa sa GFIs.

1436
01:45:20,600 --> 01:45:27,600
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: And I believe the GCG is open for further dialogue regarding this matter, Madam Sponsor.

1437
01:45:27,600 --> 01:45:29,520
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Because we really have to clarify this.

1438
01:45:30,580 --> 01:45:47,580
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Now, Madam Sponsor, ilapag po natin ang mga katotohanan dahil hindi pwedeng ginagamit ng GCG ang salitang standardization bilang lisensya para agawin.

1439
01:45:47,580 --> 01:45:52,860
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Actually, pag-agaw yun eh. Yun yung principle of non-diminution of benefits. Ibinigay na.

1440
01:45:53,780 --> 01:45:57,580
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang mga karapatang dekada ng pinakikinabangan ng mga manggagawa.

1441
01:45:58,180 --> 01:45:59,880
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, ito po yung binabanggit ko kanina.

1442
01:46:00,580 --> 01:46:07,740
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Records clearly show that Pag-ibig has provided an educational assistance benefit since 1986

1443
01:46:07,740 --> 01:46:20,000
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: and a provident fund with a 45% employer counterpart that was explicitly approved by the President back in 1994.

1444
01:46:21,000 --> 01:46:25,800
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Sa PDIC naman, malinaw sa 2011 payrolls nila,

1445
01:46:25,800 --> 01:46:37,100
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: the exact same year, RA 10149 was passed, na tumatanggap na ang mga empleyado nila ng 14th month pay and medical allowances.

1446
01:46:38,500 --> 01:46:47,620
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, because of the existence, itong pinag-uusapan natin na CPCS 1 and CPCS 2, yan po yung mga nawala.

1447
01:46:47,720 --> 01:46:50,520
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang daming nawala eh sa mga manggagawa sa GFIs.

1448
01:46:50,520 --> 01:46:54,520
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: And in fact, if you are going to ask workers in the GFIs,

1449
01:46:55,800 --> 01:47:00,340
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: isa lang sinasabi nila, ayaw namin itong CPCS 1 and CPCS 2.

1450
01:47:01,080 --> 01:47:07,360
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, Madam Sponsor, these provident funds were legally established decades before.

1451
01:47:07,500 --> 01:47:10,300
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, wala pa ng GCG, meron ng provident fund.

1452
01:47:11,200 --> 01:47:14,680
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: At meron ng arrangement, 45% nga in an example eh.

1453
01:47:15,540 --> 01:47:19,300
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, complete with presidential and statutory backing.

1454
01:47:19,300 --> 01:47:25,260
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, bakit pilit pinapatay ng GCG ang ipo ng mga manggagawa?

1455
01:47:25,800 --> 01:47:38,440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang ibig sabihin po ba ng standardization for GCG ay katumbas ng diminution?

1456
01:47:38,900 --> 01:47:41,500
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Definitely, alam ko po, sasabihin ng GCG, hindi.

1457
01:47:42,100 --> 01:47:43,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: But that is the effect.

1458
01:47:43,160 --> 01:47:44,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you.

1459
01:48:25,800 --> 01:48:35,340
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, well, as for the GCG, well, yung, this would be compensated by the monthly,

1460
01:48:35,520 --> 01:48:37,120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: like the higher monthly compensation.

1461
01:48:37,360 --> 01:48:46,380
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Yun. Medyo hindi po katanggap-tanggap yung sagot ng GCG that it will be compensated by higher or whatever.

1462
01:48:47,320 --> 01:48:52,660
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kasi nga, matagal na itong ini-enjoy ng mga manggagawa sa GFIs.

1463
01:48:53,240 --> 01:48:55,500
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: In the section 11 nga,

1464
01:48:55,800 --> 01:49:08,580
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, papaano ngayon yan, Madam Sponsor, Mr. Speaker?

1465
01:49:10,600 --> 01:49:17,560
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kasi mukhang tinitindigan pa rin ng GCG na okay lang na ang daming nawalang mga abis,

1466
01:49:18,140 --> 01:49:21,380
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ang daming mga nawalang mga ini-enjoy na ng mga manggagawa sa GFIs.

1467
01:49:21,380 --> 01:49:25,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: In fact, they are actually listening sa conversation po.

1468
01:49:25,800 --> 01:49:27,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, natin nga yun, Madam Sponsor, Mr. Speaker.

1469
01:49:28,540 --> 01:49:37,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, can the GCG commit today that they will respect the vested rights of these employees

1470
01:49:37,020 --> 01:49:45,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: and immediately approve the reinstatement requests for these provident funds pending the resolution?

1471
01:49:45,420 --> 01:49:54,860
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kung meron mang mga legal battles, makukuha rin ba namin ang commitment ng GCG na makipagpulong po sa mga manggagawa ng GFIs?

1472
01:49:55,800 --> 01:50:01,900
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kasi sila po ang ultimate beneficiary and casualty of what we are talking about right now.

1473
01:50:02,640 --> 01:50:05,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, ang gusto po ng mga manggagawa sa GFIs ay kalinawan.

1474
01:50:06,780 --> 01:50:11,180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So, will we get that commitment from GCG, Madam Sponsor?

1475
01:50:12,100 --> 01:50:13,460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

1476
01:50:14,340 --> 01:50:18,220
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The GCG is, well, upon the assurance of our good chairperson,

1477
01:50:18,640 --> 01:50:24,080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: is willing also to present the data that they've run assessments,

1478
01:50:24,540 --> 01:50:25,580
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: they've arrived at...

1479
01:50:25,800 --> 01:50:31,780
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: different numbers that give justification to their stance.

1480
01:50:31,960 --> 01:50:36,520
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: But, of course, with the help, of course, of my distinguished colleague,

1481
01:50:36,800 --> 01:50:39,540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Honorable San Fernando, personally this representation,

1482
01:50:39,980 --> 01:50:44,820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: let's facilitate the dialogue between the GCG and our members from the Labor Center.

1483
01:50:44,820 --> 01:50:50,480
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you very much to my good friend, the sponsor, Congresswoman Bella Swan Singh.

1484
01:50:51,260 --> 01:50:54,080
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kasi gusto natin at the end of the day, ma-resolve ba itong problema ito?

1485
01:50:54,080 --> 01:50:56,880
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kasi the last thing that we would like to happen,

1486
01:50:57,700 --> 01:51:01,520
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: pag itong lahat ng GFIs, pitong GFIs,

1487
01:51:02,300 --> 01:51:05,540
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: yung mga manggagawa nito ay hindi nakapagtimpe,

1488
01:51:06,500 --> 01:51:07,540
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: lalabas tong mga to.

1489
01:51:08,820 --> 01:51:11,560
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: That is, yun yung gusto natin, hanggat maaari,

1490
01:51:11,680 --> 01:51:16,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: ayaw natin tumuntong sa isang sitwasyon na hindi natin makukontrol

1491
01:51:16,840 --> 01:51:23,360
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: dahil very personal at malalim ang hugot ng mga manggagawa sa GFIs

1492
01:51:24,080 --> 01:51:28,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: dito sa mga nawalang allowances, benefits, and incentives.

1493
01:51:29,100 --> 01:51:34,420
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: And for so long, hindi nila nakukuha yung sagot from GCG.

1494
01:51:34,560 --> 01:51:41,060
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: And it is a welcome development that the sponsor is assuring this representation

1495
01:51:41,060 --> 01:51:46,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: that through the chairperson of GCG ay magkakaroon tayo ng pag-uusap.

1496
01:51:46,160 --> 01:51:52,620
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Now, on to the third question, part of my question.

1497
01:51:54,080 --> 01:51:57,580
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Malinaw po na nakasaad sa saligang batas natin,

1498
01:51:57,680 --> 01:52:02,620
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: and in fact, this has been enshrined in labor laws and other relevant labor laws,

1499
01:52:03,260 --> 01:52:09,220
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: yung karapatan ng mga manggagawa na organisahin yung kanyang sarili

1500
01:52:09,220 --> 01:52:14,120
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: at makipag-negosasyon o makipagtawaran sa kanyang employer.

1501
01:52:14,940 --> 01:52:20,440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kung sa pampublikong sektor, collective negotiation ang tawag.

1502
01:52:20,440 --> 01:52:22,420
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So sa pribadong sektor, collective bargaining.

1503
01:52:24,080 --> 01:52:30,140
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: In fact, sa Article 13, Section 3, at maging sa Executive Order No. 180,

1504
01:52:31,200 --> 01:52:34,440
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: garantisado ang karapatan ng lahat ng manggagawa,

1505
01:52:35,080 --> 01:52:38,800
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: kasama ang mga manggagawa sa pampublikong sektor,

1506
01:52:39,660 --> 01:52:43,640
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: pagdating sa usapin ng self-organization and collective negotiation.

1507
01:52:43,640 --> 01:52:46,640
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Pero ito po yung malaking katanungan.

1508
01:52:47,760 --> 01:52:49,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: In CPCS 1 and CPCS 2,

1509
01:52:51,060 --> 01:52:53,580
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: eh, pinoprohibit.

1510
01:52:54,080 --> 01:53:02,980
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Yung mga GOCC boards na magkaroon ng collective negotiation with its workers.

1511
01:53:03,580 --> 01:53:08,200
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So there is an absolute blanket prohibition.

1512
01:53:09,340 --> 01:53:13,500
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So papaano po, so does the Commission honestly believe that

1513
01:53:13,500 --> 01:53:19,300
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: this absolute blanket prohibition on negotiating every single economic,

1514
01:53:20,060 --> 01:53:23,700
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: so yung economic provisions po ang pinatutungkulan Madam Sponsor,

1515
01:53:24,460 --> 01:53:27,680
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: so negotiating every single economic term,

1516
01:53:28,500 --> 01:53:33,200
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: is consistent with the constitutional guarantee of self-organization?

1517
01:54:31,380 --> 01:54:49,060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, as for the GCG, there is recognition of their right to self-organization. However, in terms of bargaining for economic terms, apparently there are already a long list of Supreme Court rulings that...

1518
01:54:49,060 --> 01:54:51,860
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: What is that specific Supreme Court ruling?

1519
01:54:54,080 --> 01:55:13,480
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: I'd like to reiterate. Constitutional guarantee, yung collective negotiation. So ano po yung sa Supreme Court ruling?

1520
01:55:24,080 --> 01:55:37,020
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: If I'm allowed to enumerate, this is for your GSIS Family Bank Employees Union v. Villanueva, JR number 210773.

1521
01:55:37,760 --> 01:55:39,940
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: 210, JR number 210.

1522
01:55:39,940 --> 01:55:53,800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 210773, a rule that may not negotiate with their officers and employees the economic terms of their collective bargaining agreements.

1523
01:55:54,080 --> 01:56:03,030
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And then for another Supreme Court ruling, PNCC versus NLRC, G.R. number 24...

1524
01:56:03,030 --> 01:56:06,370
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Anong kaso po ?yan, Madam Sponsor?

1525
01:56:06,370 --> 01:56:07,380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: PNCC.

1526
01:56:07,380 --> 01:56:08,360
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Okay, okay.

1527
01:56:08,360 --> 01:56:21,040
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yeah, PNCC versus NLRC, G.R. number 248401, said that with the subsequent enactment of RA 10149,

1528
01:56:21,040 --> 01:56:23,800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: PNCC may no longer grant this benefit.

1529
01:56:24,080 --> 01:56:27,500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Without persecuring the requisite authority of the President.

1530
01:56:28,500 --> 01:56:31,560
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Without the authority of the President.

1531
01:56:31,760 --> 01:56:31,980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

1532
01:56:32,500 --> 01:56:39,220
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Hayaan niyo po, Madam Sponsor, na reviewin din ang kinatawang ito, yung binanggit niyo po na jurisprudence on this matter.

1533
01:56:39,760 --> 01:56:42,180
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kaya po maganda nga na magkakaroon tayo ng dialogo.

1534
01:56:42,180 --> 01:56:48,100
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So as to reconcile our reading on this particular case.

1535
01:56:48,800 --> 01:56:53,760
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Kasi napakalinaw na tila baga nadidefeat na.

1536
01:56:54,080 --> 01:57:04,020
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Ang constitutional guarantee pagdating sa collective negotiation, medyo mabigat po yun.

1537
01:57:04,760 --> 01:57:14,000
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Nadagok sa mga union ng mga manggagawa dahil the reason of existence po ng mga union ng mga manggagawa,

1538
01:57:14,000 --> 01:57:23,460
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: may it be in private or public sector, ay para may abante yung mga panawagan tungkol sa pagdadagdag ng sahod,

1539
01:57:23,580 --> 01:57:24,000
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: mga benepisyon.

1540
01:57:24,080 --> 01:57:26,080
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Yun nga po, yung abis na tinatawag.

1541
01:57:27,260 --> 01:57:35,780
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So marami pong katanungan pa na gustong himayin ang kinatawang ito, pero dahil limitado po ang oras natin,

1542
01:57:36,480 --> 01:57:42,080
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: will we get that commitment again from the distinguished sponsor and the GCG through its chairperson,

1543
01:57:43,700 --> 01:57:53,820
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: for us to sit down together and have an honest to goodness talk and dialogue about this matter and questions of workers in the GFIs?

1544
01:57:54,080 --> 01:57:54,740
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Madam Sponsor?

1545
01:57:56,740 --> 01:58:09,960
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, we reaffirm the commitment and I was also informed by our good chairperson that this coming Friday, next Friday,

1546
01:58:10,460 --> 01:58:17,120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: may meeting daw po with the labor groups firm, GFIs.

1547
01:58:17,420 --> 01:58:22,960
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: Thank you, Madam Sponsor and through the chairperson of GCG for affirming.

1548
01:58:24,080 --> 01:58:31,460
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: That commitment, dahil ako rin po ang kinatawang ito ay nais malinawan sa napakaraming mga tanong.

1549
01:58:32,080 --> 01:58:39,540
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: So thank you, Madam Sponsor, to my good friend and asahan ko po yung pagtutulungan natin on this matter.

1550
01:58:40,100 --> 01:58:53,140
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: And with that, Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor, there being no other member from the minority to interpolate for the budget of GCG,

1551
01:58:53,140 --> 01:58:53,840
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: I move.

1552
01:58:54,080 --> 01:59:06,160
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: To terminate the period of sponsorship and debate for the plenary consideration of the budget of the Governance Commission for GOCCs for Fiscal Year 2027.

1553
01:59:06,400 --> 01:59:08,080
Rep. Elijah Rumbaoa San Fernando: I so move, Mr. Speaker.

1554
01:59:08,600 --> 01:59:09,800
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: What does the House say?

1555
01:59:09,980 --> 01:59:10,720
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Majority Leader.

1556
01:59:11,340 --> 01:59:23,940
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, on the part of the majority, we join the minority to terminate the period of interpellation in the Governance Commission for GOCCs.

1557
01:59:24,080 --> 01:59:33,600
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: There is a joint motion to terminate the interpellations on the proposed budget of the Governance Commission for GOCCs.

1558
01:59:34,240 --> 01:59:35,260
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Is there any objection?

1559
01:59:36,520 --> 01:59:37,520
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: The Chair hears none.

1560
01:59:38,340 --> 01:59:46,180
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: The interpellation on the proposed budget of the Governance Commission for GOCCs is hereby terminated.

1561
01:59:46,940 --> 01:59:47,700
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Congratulations.

1562
01:59:50,080 --> 01:59:51,100
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Majority Leader.

1563
01:59:52,750 --> 01:59:54,060
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, I move.

1564
01:59:54,080 --> 01:59:58,680
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: To consider the proposed budget of the Mindanao Development Authority.

1565
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:05,780
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Is there any objection? The Chair hears none. Motion is approved. Majority Leader.

1566
02:00:06,400 --> 02:00:24,300
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, may we acknowledge the heads and officials of the Mindanao Development Authority, Chairperson Leo Magno, Usec Janet Lopoz, Asec Romeo Montenegro. I so move, Mr. Speaker.

1567
02:00:24,960 --> 02:00:39,740
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: To the family of the Mindanao Development Authority, headed by the Chairperson, Secretary Leo Tereso Magno, welcome to the House of Representatives. Majority Leader.

1568
02:00:40,840 --> 02:00:53,330
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, I move that you recognize the Honorable Nicanor Briones, Vice Chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations to sponsor the proposed budget of the Mindanao Development Authority.

1569
02:00:54,170 --> 02:01:00,280
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: The Honorable Representative Niki Briones is recognized. Please proceed.

1570
02:01:01,850 --> 02:01:03,360
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

1571
02:01:04,220 --> 02:01:07,300
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Dear colleagues, ladies and gentlemen, good evening.

1572
02:01:08,680 --> 02:01:20,320
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: I rise today to sponsor the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget of the Mindanao Development Authority, headed by Secretary Leo Tereso Magno.

1573
02:01:21,500 --> 02:01:24,100
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Mindanao Development Authority is mandated.

1574
02:01:24,120 --> 02:01:45,340
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: By virtue of Republic Act No. 9996, to promote, coordinate, and facilitate the socio-economic development of Mindanao through an integrated approach promoting trade, tourism, investment, private enterprises, and peace.

1575
02:01:45,840 --> 02:01:54,100
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: It also serves as the permanent Philippine Coordinating Office for the Brunei Darussalam-Indonesia-Malaysia-Philippines East ASEAN Growth Area.

1576
02:01:54,120 --> 02:02:15,840
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: It acts as the Secretariat for the Mindanao Power Monitoring Committee, Mindanao River Basin Management Council, NTF-ELCAC, and Cabinet Officer for Regional Development and Security in Mindanao.

1577
02:02:15,840 --> 02:02:22,840
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: It also implements critical strategic programs for the Mindanao.

1578
02:02:24,120 --> 02:02:33,720
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Such as the Project RIBER, which helps local government units develop, rehabilitate, and maintain its water supply infrastructure.

1579
02:02:35,060 --> 02:02:53,700
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: These programs are aligned with the Mindanao Agenda, which aims to achieve inclusive economic recovery, sustain green growth, build resilience, and strengthen peace and development for an improved quality of life for every Mindanao citizen.

1580
02:02:54,120 --> 02:03:25,710
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: [unclear] by 2030. For this, we respectfully seek this Chamber's support to consider and approve the proposed budget of the Mindanao Development Authority for fiscal year 2027, amounting to ₱272,435,000. Together, let us help a better Mindanao. Thank you very much, and I now welcome any questions from our colleagues.

1581
02:03:26,840 --> 02:03:30,620
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Thank you, Honorable Briones. Majority Leader.

1582
02:03:30,620 --> 02:03:35,650
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Presley De Jesus for his interpellation.

1583
02:03:35,970 --> 02:03:42,550
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: The Honorable Presley De Jesus of Party-list PHILRECA is recognized. Please proceed.

1584
02:03:43,660 --> 02:03:51,540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. Of course, to the distinguished sponsor, this is about the Mindanao Energy Security.

1585
02:03:51,540 --> 02:04:06,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Question. Mr. Speaker, this is the sponsor. Based on the projects, Minda has identified reliable and affordable electricity necessary for their success and sustainability.

1586
02:04:36,720 --> 02:04:38,340
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: What's your question?

1587
02:04:38,340 --> 02:05:04,070
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay, let me repeat my question. Based on the projects, MinDA has identified reliable and affordable electricity necessary for their success and sustainability. In short, naka-rely po kayo sa success ng the Mindanao project, yung affordable electricity for their success and sustainability. Yes or no?

1588
02:05:04,540 --> 02:05:07,380
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yes, distinguished colleague.

1589
02:05:07,380 --> 02:05:21,460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. Does Minda recognize electricity as a foundational requirement for Mindanao's industrial, agricultural, commercial, educational, health, and social development?

1590
02:05:21,540 --> 02:05:24,960
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yes, distinguished colleague.

1591
02:05:25,620 --> 02:05:33,280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Can MinDA describe what they know about the Agus-Pulangi hydropower complex?

1592
02:05:34,400 --> 02:05:37,140
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yes, Your Honor.

1593
02:05:40,140 --> 02:05:43,700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sir, can you describe what they know?

1594
02:05:43,700 --> 02:05:50,860
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: We support all our efforts for the rehabilitation of the Agus Pulangi.

1595
02:05:51,540 --> 02:05:59,000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, are you familiar with the Agus-Pulangi hydropower complex?

1596
02:05:59,940 --> 02:06:02,300
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yes, distinguished colleague.

1597
02:06:03,300 --> 02:06:10,420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Alam niyo po, ang Agus-Pulangi, yan po yung matagal na pong pinagkukunan, source of energy sa Mindanao.

1598
02:06:10,840 --> 02:06:15,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That's why Congressman Sergio Dagooc, passionate siya pagdating po rito.

1599
02:06:15,940 --> 02:06:21,520
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, ang tanong ko po, because as we know, marami.

1600
02:06:21,540 --> 02:06:25,680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Marami po nag-aahangad sa Agus-Pulangi na ma-privatize.

1601
02:06:26,660 --> 02:06:41,440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, do the Mindanao officers ng Mindanao Development Authority, are you in favor of, on record, are you in favor of privatizing Agus-Pulangi?

1602
02:06:46,440 --> 02:06:49,380
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague.

1603
02:06:51,540 --> 02:06:58,600
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: What the Mindanao Development Authority wants is rehabilitation, not privatization.

1604
02:06:59,240 --> 02:07:05,100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, in short, you're in favor or you're not in favor of privatizing Agus-Pulangi?

1605
02:07:05,220 --> 02:07:07,640
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: No, no. Mindanao is not in favor.

1606
02:07:07,840 --> 02:07:08,840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, you're not in favor?

1607
02:07:09,680 --> 02:07:10,420
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yes, Your Honor.

1608
02:07:10,420 --> 02:07:17,360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Second, so, as we know, that Agus-Pulangi hydropower needs rehabilitation.

1609
02:07:19,780 --> 02:07:20,580
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yeah, yes.

1610
02:07:21,540 --> 02:07:41,620
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: As of now, the capacity of the Agus-Pulangi hydropower plant is 1,000 megawatts and it's only running 600 to 700 megawatts, distinguished colleague.

1611
02:07:42,960 --> 02:07:47,440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, in short, again, let me do some fun facts.

1612
02:07:47,440 --> 02:07:51,240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor.

1613
02:07:51,540 --> 02:08:04,840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The National Power Corporation identifies the Agus-Pulangi complexes as having a combined installed capacity of 982 megawatts

1614
02:08:04,840 --> 02:08:10,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and supplying more than 50% of Mindanao's electricity requirements.

1615
02:08:10,180 --> 02:08:14,100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Alam po natin kung ano po ang kalagayan ng Agus-Pulangi.

1616
02:08:14,600 --> 02:08:18,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Dito po nanggagaling kalahati po ng supply sa Mindanao.

1617
02:08:19,120 --> 02:08:20,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kaya, pansinin niyo po.

1618
02:08:21,540 --> 02:08:23,840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Bisayas, nagkakaroon ng yellow alert.

1619
02:08:24,820 --> 02:08:30,740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Even na Luzon, pero ang Bisayas, ang Mindanao ay bihira po because of Agus-Pulangi.

1620
02:08:33,000 --> 02:08:47,520
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Does Mindanao Development Authority agree that preserving affordable and reliable access to this renewable energy resource is essential to Mindanao development?

1621
02:08:48,220 --> 02:08:49,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Do you recognize po yan?

1622
02:08:49,780 --> 02:08:51,520
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Definitely, Mr. Speaker.

1623
02:08:51,540 --> 02:08:53,540
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Distinguished colleague.

1624
02:08:55,160 --> 02:08:55,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you.

1625
02:08:56,860 --> 02:09:07,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: If electricity is vital to Mindanao's development and Agus-Pulangi is a major government-owned source of electricity,

1626
02:09:08,840 --> 02:09:16,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: what precisely is Mindanao's position on private participation in its rehabilitation operation and management arrangement?

1627
02:09:16,920 --> 02:09:18,140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ano ba yung arrangement nyo?

1628
02:09:18,260 --> 02:09:21,500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kasi, ano po, rehabilitate na.

1629
02:09:21,540 --> 02:09:24,280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ano po ang operation and management?

1630
02:09:24,620 --> 02:09:26,840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ano po ang arrangement po natin dito?

1631
02:09:49,640 --> 02:09:50,960
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Mr. Speaker,

1632
02:09:51,540 --> 02:10:17,340
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Distinguished colleague, iba ang ahensya na mag-iimplement ng privatization. Yung PSALM ang siyang mag-iimplement ng privatization [unclear].

1633
02:10:17,340 --> 02:10:27,340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, Mr. Speaker, medyo gusto ko lang linawin ito. Are we going to privatize ang Agus-Pulangi o yung kanilang rehabilitation lang?

1634
02:10:27,900 --> 02:10:29,760
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: It's only for rehabilitation.

1635
02:10:30,020 --> 02:10:44,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay. So, malinaw po, Mr. Speaker, on record, the Agus-Pulangi will not be privatized but only yung rehabilitation ang ibibigay sa private. Tama ba ako doon?

1636
02:10:46,100 --> 02:10:46,980
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Tama po.

1637
02:10:47,340 --> 02:10:51,640
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Mr. Speaker, yun ang gagawin.

1638
02:10:51,820 --> 02:10:54,680
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yun ang gagawin, Mr. Speaker.

1639
02:10:54,680 --> 02:10:57,560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay. This is very important.

1640
02:10:58,380 --> 02:11:17,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Section 47F of EPIRA excluded Agus-Pulangi from the generation assets initially privatized, provided that the ownership will be transferred to PSALM and the hydropower complexes will continue to be operated

1641
02:11:17,340 --> 02:11:28,380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: by NPC. It further states that privatization is left to PSALM's discretion in consultation with Congress.

1642
02:11:30,180 --> 02:11:30,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Do you agree with that?

1643
02:11:30,920 --> 02:11:32,780
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

1644
02:11:33,340 --> 02:11:37,580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: We have to kasi. Nasa EPIRA law too. Section 47F, no?

1645
02:11:38,240 --> 02:11:46,260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor, meron po bang naganap na konsultasyon sa Kongreso?

1646
02:11:46,260 --> 02:11:47,260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, patuloy.

1647
02:11:47,340 --> 02:12:02,980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kung tungkol sa rehabilitation ng Agus-Pulangi, as far as I know, wala po akong alam na [unclear] hindi po ito kasama sa mandato ng Mindanao [unclear].

1648
02:12:04,180 --> 02:12:17,060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ang gusto ko lang po dito malaman ay kung ano po talaga ang position ng Minda sa pangangalagaan natin sa nag-iisa na lamang na government-owned.

1649
02:12:17,340 --> 02:12:27,820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ito na lang po ang natitira. Kasi lahat po ng generation naibenta na ng PSALM. Ito na lang po ang kaisa-isa, ang Agus-Pulangi sa Mindanao.

1650
02:12:28,580 --> 02:12:39,780
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: As the Development Authority in Mindanao, would you allow the vital and strategic energy asset na mapunta na lamang sa kamay ng private corporation?

1651
02:12:39,780 --> 02:12:46,780
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, you said you are not willing to turn it over or to sell it to private corporation.

1652
02:12:47,340 --> 02:12:48,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Am I right?

1653
02:12:49,380 --> 02:12:55,720
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague, tama po yun.

1654
02:12:57,100 --> 02:12:59,160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes, tama. Hindi natin ibebenta.

1655
02:12:59,560 --> 02:13:00,760
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Hindi pwedeng ibebenta.

1656
02:13:00,980 --> 02:13:06,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That would be my five times na I asked you and you said yes, na hindi ibebenta. Thank you for that.

1657
02:13:07,600 --> 02:13:08,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Follow-up question, Mr. Speaker.

1658
02:13:10,100 --> 02:13:16,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: May ginawa po ba ang MinDA para makasiguro na ang mga tao sa Agus, sa Lanao, sa Bukidnon

1659
02:13:17,340 --> 02:13:26,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: sa Iligan o sa iba pang mga apektadong komunidad na kasama sila sa decision-making patungkol dito sa Agus-Pulangi?

1660
02:13:26,880 --> 02:13:32,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sigurado po ako ay importante po itong issue na ito para sa ating mga local communities.

1661
02:13:32,780 --> 02:13:38,640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Have you ever engaged the people from Lanao, Bukidno, even in Iligan?

1662
02:13:39,320 --> 02:13:44,080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Pagdating po rito, nagkaroon ba ng public consultation? Even yung rehabilitation lang?

1663
02:13:47,340 --> 02:13:54,700
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Considering that Minda is a member of the Power Monitoring Committee, nagkaroon po ng consultation.

1664
02:13:55,660 --> 02:13:59,080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So there was consultation happen?

1665
02:13:59,960 --> 02:14:01,280
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

1666
02:14:01,280 --> 02:14:02,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: When? Where?

1667
02:14:11,980 --> 02:14:16,660
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague, every year, nagkakaroon ng...

1668
02:14:17,340 --> 02:14:26,000
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Mindanao Power Summit, kasama ang lahat ng stakeholders sa summit.

1669
02:14:26,000 --> 02:14:42,220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So every year, there's a consultation. Was the consultation included or it being mentioned, the privatization or even the rehabilitation of Agus-Pulangi? Kasama po ba yan

1670
02:14:42,220 --> 02:14:43,220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Pagkaano kayo?

1671
02:14:44,160 --> 02:14:45,220
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Kasama, kasama yung...

1672
02:14:45,980 --> 02:14:47,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Habang nagkakaroon kayo?

1673
02:14:47,340 --> 02:14:48,060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In February na summit.

1674
02:14:49,220 --> 02:14:51,280
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Kasama yung rehabilitation?

1675
02:14:52,440 --> 02:14:53,560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And the privatization.

1676
02:15:00,000 --> 02:15:08,020
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: At tuloy-tuloy ang pag-uusap tungkol sa Agus-Pulangi, kasama ang Department of Energy.

1677
02:15:08,440 --> 02:15:15,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: When you say continuous dialogue, ano ho yung pinag-uusapan?

1678
02:15:17,580 --> 02:15:19,320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In privatization ho ba o hindi?

1679
02:15:28,130 --> 02:15:33,140
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Only privatization of maintenance and rehabilitation.

1680
02:15:33,140 --> 02:15:44,100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So ano ho ang sabi ng mga tao from Bukidnon, Iligan, and Lanao? Are they in favor of privatization of Agus-Pulangi?

1681
02:16:02,300 --> 02:16:10,960
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague, ang gusto ng taong bayan ay rehabilitation.

1682
02:16:10,960 --> 02:16:12,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Rehabilitation?

1683
02:16:12,120 --> 02:16:17,520
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: At continuously makapag-serve ang Agus-Pulangi.

1684
02:16:17,520 --> 02:16:18,870
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The Mindanao people wanted?

1685
02:16:18,870 --> 02:16:20,020
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: One hundred percent.

1686
02:16:20,510 --> 02:16:23,600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Rehabilitation, but not privatization of Agus-Pulangi.

1687
02:16:23,600 --> 02:16:31,760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, for that. At least natutuwa ako, lalo na si Kong Serge Dagooc na nanonood ngayon sa atin.

1688
02:16:32,500 --> 02:16:38,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Dahil nandun siya sa Mindanao ngayon. Umiiyak siguro habang pinanonood tayo na sa Agus-Pulangi yung tao.

1689
02:16:39,280 --> 02:16:43,200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: He's a very dedicated person, being a lineman himself.

1690
02:16:43,200 --> 02:16:46,220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: My next question.

1691
02:16:49,320 --> 02:16:58,080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Given Mindanao Development Authority mandate to promote, coordinate, and facilitate Mindanao's socioeconomic development,

1692
02:16:58,840 --> 02:17:12,140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: is the agency truly protecting the interests of Mindanao when it supports or tolerates an arrangement that may place a major government-owned source of electricity under private control?

1693
02:17:12,140 --> 02:17:18,100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I guess, nasagot mo naman na ito, so we don't have to answer that. At least a sign of relief.

1694
02:17:19,320 --> 02:17:34,540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Did MinDA ever submit a written recommendation to the President, DOE, PSALM, NPC, even Congress, or any other responsible body concerning Agus-Pulangi?

1695
02:17:34,540 --> 02:17:42,280
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

1696
02:17:42,280 --> 02:17:49,280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Does that recommendation prioritize the long-term welfare of Mindanao residents?

1697
02:17:49,320 --> 02:17:53,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Over short-term fiscal proceeds or private investor returns?

1698
02:17:55,320 --> 02:17:57,100
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Yes, Your Honor.

1699
02:17:58,180 --> 02:18:18,320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, Mr. Speaker, before Congress approves its proposed fiscal year 2027 budget, Mindanao Development Authority should assure this August body that it is genuinely prioritizing the welfare of the people of Mindanao.

1700
02:18:19,320 --> 02:18:24,000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And is committed to the inclusive and sustainable development of the region.

1701
02:18:24,240 --> 02:18:43,880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That commitment must be demonstrated not only through plans, meetings, and policy statements, but through the protection of Mindanao's strategic public assets, particularly Agus-Pulangi.

1702
02:18:43,880 --> 02:18:48,880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: These facilities are essential to Mindanao.

1703
02:18:49,320 --> 02:18:52,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mindanao's energy security and development.

1704
02:18:52,880 --> 02:19:10,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: They must remain subject to public accountability and must not be placed under the control of private entities at the expense of consumers, electric, cooperatives, host communities, and the broader public interest.

1705
02:19:10,300 --> 02:19:19,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Accordingly, the Mindanao Development Authority should clearly and unequivocally state that it will not support

1706
02:19:19,320 --> 02:19:37,440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: any arrangement that transfers effective control of Agus-Pulangi to private corporations without transparent justification, congressional consultation, strong consumer safeguards, and continuing public control.

1707
02:19:38,540 --> 02:19:48,380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mindanao should also assure this committee that it is not siding with private corporations for their own commercial or financial interests.

1708
02:19:49,320 --> 02:19:56,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The recommendation must be based solely on its statutory mandate and the long-term welfare of the people of Mindanao.

1709
02:19:57,920 --> 02:20:07,240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Minda should have a clear commitment to remain independent, transparent, accountable, and firmly aligned with the people of Mindanao.

1710
02:20:07,240 --> 02:20:21,380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Before I end my interpellation, Mr. Speaker, Congressman Dagooc and I strongly oppose the privatization of Agus-Pulangi.

1711
02:20:21,840 --> 02:20:28,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yan na lang po ang nag-iisang generation po ng ating gobyerno.

1712
02:20:29,120 --> 02:20:35,080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sana manatili pong yan government-owned para po sa ating mga kababayan sa Mindanao.

1713
02:20:35,080 --> 02:20:37,220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, thank you very much, Mr. Speaker.

1714
02:20:37,240 --> 02:20:47,060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And of course, to the good-looking sponsor and to the rest of Mindanao Development Authority family.

