Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: hindi raw kailangan na

4126
04:58:10,520 --> 04:58:13,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: makuha ang kanilang consent.

4127
04:58:13,520 --> 04:58:16,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi sila covered ng IPRA requirements, no?

4128
04:58:22,200 --> 04:58:24,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yamang may mga serious concerns pa po tayo rito.

4129
04:58:24,520 --> 04:58:25,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Madam Speaker,

4130
04:58:25,520 --> 04:58:30,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I move to suspend deliberation on the proposed budget

4131
04:58:30,520 --> 04:58:33,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: of the Bases Conversion and Development Authority

4132
04:58:33,520 --> 04:58:36,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: to allow the consideration of the proposed budget

4133
04:58:36,520 --> 04:58:39,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: of the other remaining agencies scheduled today.

4134
04:58:39,520 --> 04:58:40,520
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Madam Speaker,

4135
04:58:40,520 --> 04:58:41,520
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: on the part of the majority,

4136
04:58:41,520 --> 04:58:43,520
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: we join the minority in the motion.

4137
04:58:43,520 --> 04:58:45,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: There is a joint motion to suspend consideration

4138
04:58:45,520 --> 04:58:46,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: of the proposed budget of

4139
04:58:46,520 --> 04:58:48,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Bases Conversion and Development Authority.

4140
04:58:48,520 --> 04:58:49,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Do you hear an objection?

4141
04:58:50,520 --> 04:58:51,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Hearing none,

4142
04:58:51,520 --> 04:58:53,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: the joint motion is approved.

4143
04:58:56,520 --> 04:58:58,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Consideration of the proposed budget

4144
04:58:58,520 --> 04:59:00,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: of BCDA is suspended.

4145
04:59:00,520 --> 04:59:01,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader?

4146
04:59:01,520 --> 04:59:02,520
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Madam Speaker,

4147
04:59:02,520 --> 04:59:04,520
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: I move to consider the proposed budget

4148
04:59:04,520 --> 04:59:07,520
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: of the Subic Bay Metropolitan Authority.

4149
04:59:09,520 --> 04:59:11,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: May we also request the Majority Leader

4150
04:59:11,520 --> 04:59:14,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: to move for the recognition

4151
04:59:14,520 --> 04:59:16,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: of the sponsor and the interpolator.

4152
04:59:17,520 --> 04:59:18,520
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Madam Speaker,

4153
04:59:18,520 --> 04:59:20,520
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: may we acknowledge the officials

4154
04:59:20,520 --> 04:59:21,520
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: of the Subic Bay...

4155
04:59:21,830 --> 04:59:22,930
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session suspended.

4156
04:59:36,650 --> 04:59:37,630
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Session resumed.

4157
04:59:39,520 --> 04:59:40,520
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Madam Speaker,

4158
04:59:40,520 --> 04:59:41,520
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: may we acknowledge the officials

4159
04:59:41,520 --> 04:59:43,520
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: of the Subic Bay Metropolitan Authority,

4160
04:59:43,520 --> 04:59:46,520
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Chairman and Administrator Eduardo Aliño.

4161
04:59:46,520 --> 04:59:48,240
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: I so move, Madam Speaker.

4162
04:59:50,860 --> 04:59:51,680
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Madam Speaker,

4163
04:59:51,940 --> 04:59:52,940
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: I move that we recognize

4164
04:59:52,940 --> 04:59:56,880
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: the Honorable Bella Vanessa Swancing,

4165
04:59:56,880 --> 05:00:01,820
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Vice Chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations, to sponsor the proposed budget of the Subic Bay.

4166
05:00:01,840 --> 05:00:08,100
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: There is a motion to consider the proposed budget of the Subic Bay Metropolitan Authority

4167
05:00:08,100 --> 05:00:13,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and for this purpose, the Hon. Bella Swansing is recognized to sponsor said measure

4168
05:00:13,520 --> 05:00:16,820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: and the Hon. Rene Luis Co as interpellator.

4169
05:00:16,960 --> 05:00:17,660
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Please proceed.

4170
05:00:19,960 --> 05:00:24,280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, good evening.

4171
05:00:24,280 --> 05:00:33,240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And will the sponsor be open to answer a few questions in relation to the budget

4172
05:00:33,240 --> 05:00:36,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and the policies of Subic Bay Metropolitan Authority?

4173
05:00:37,440 --> 05:00:38,820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, gladly, Madam Speaker.

4174
05:00:39,140 --> 05:00:46,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay. Madam Speaker, good sponsor, we note that under the watch of the current administration,

4175
05:00:47,180 --> 05:00:53,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: SBMA has allowed 234 containers of suspected e-waste from the United States

4176
05:00:53,760 --> 05:00:54,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to enter Subic Bay.

4177
05:00:54,280 --> 05:00:56,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Since March 2025.

4178
05:00:57,160 --> 05:01:03,500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And another 184 containers almost arrived between August and September 2026,

4179
05:01:04,120 --> 05:01:08,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: all without the prior informed consent required by the Basel Convention.

4180
05:01:08,860 --> 05:01:12,340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa ilalim po ng Basel Convention, Madam Speaker, good sponsor,

4181
05:01:12,460 --> 05:01:16,880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng e-waste amendment na pumasok sa bisa noong Enero 2025,

4182
05:01:17,820 --> 05:01:23,200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: halos lahat ng e-waste, hazardous man o hindi, ay kontrolado ng konbensyon.

4183
05:01:24,100 --> 05:01:27,800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Malinaw sa probisyon ng Article 4, subsection 5,

4184
05:01:28,580 --> 05:01:34,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: nagbabawal sa kalakalan ng basura sa isang non-party tulad ng United States.

4185
05:01:35,240 --> 05:01:41,320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: In fact, kung meron pong trade or export galing OECD countries, EU countries,

4186
05:01:41,320 --> 05:01:47,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: or Liechtenstein, dapat limited lang sa kanila at hindi po sa labas nito mangyari.

4187
05:01:48,080 --> 05:01:54,240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Nonetheless, there's been export of e-waste from the United States imported to the Philippines.

4188
05:01:54,280 --> 05:02:02,000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Wala rin pong anumang bilateral agreement na nagpapahintulot ng importasyon ng e-waste mula sa US papunta sa Pilipinas.

4189
05:02:02,380 --> 05:02:05,140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: This is confirmed by the Department of Foreign Affairs.

4190
05:02:05,600 --> 05:02:12,540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang umiira lamang nakasunduan ay para sa exports ng ating bansa papunta sa US, and not the other way around.

4191
05:02:13,820 --> 05:02:18,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We have heard preliminarily some defenses of SBMA,

4192
05:02:18,180 --> 05:02:22,240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and this is also what is provided in an RTC ruling,

4193
05:02:23,120 --> 05:02:23,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which allowed...

4194
05:02:24,280 --> 05:02:29,120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the activities of such trade in SBMA.

4195
05:02:29,740 --> 05:02:32,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor, my question is,

4196
05:02:33,000 --> 05:02:40,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: does being a separate customs territory as provided in law enable SBMA to circumvent,

4197
05:02:40,560 --> 05:02:45,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: or essentially not follow, ratified international treaties and agreements?

4198
05:02:54,280 --> 05:03:07,680
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, the SBMA confirms the importation of scrapped mixed metals, computer accessories, used meter, used electronics, and scrapped copper.

4199
05:03:08,160 --> 05:03:14,100
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: However, these importations, as per the SBMA, adhere to international treaties.

4200
05:03:15,180 --> 05:03:15,640
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker.

4201
05:03:16,300 --> 05:03:22,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor, ano pong reaction ng SBMA na...

4202
05:03:22,640 --> 05:03:31,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na under the Convention, and even under the implementing DNR Department Order,

4203
05:03:31,260 --> 05:03:42,400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: wala naman pong pagbubukod ng e-waste, na ito po ay separate or hindi considered as hazardous wastes.

4204
05:03:42,760 --> 05:03:51,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Hazardous wastes po siya na nililimitahan yung import-export regulation trade po nito ng Basel Convention,

4205
05:03:51,640 --> 05:03:52,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which...

4206
05:03:52,180 --> 05:04:02,680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which explicitly provides, hindi po pwedeng magkaroon ng export from a non-party to a state party.

4207
05:04:10,440 --> 05:04:11,030
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ...

4208
05:04:21,080 --> 05:04:21,920
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: What does the

4209
05:04:21,920 --> 05:04:22,540
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: sponsor say?

4210
05:04:28,120 --> 05:04:31,220
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

4211
05:04:32,320 --> 05:04:41,940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: SBMA still confirms that all importations of scrapped mixed metals are not hazardous.

4212
05:04:41,940 --> 05:04:44,120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: These are...

4213
05:04:44,120 --> 05:04:50,720
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: These all adhere to all environmental regulations.

4214
05:04:52,140 --> 05:05:06,120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor, the Basel Action Network, which maintains and checks the compliance of states with the Basel Convention,

4215
05:05:06,120 --> 05:05:18,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: found in its field investigations in both the U.S. and the Philippines, that these containers that arrived at the Subic Port from the United States,

4216
05:05:18,440 --> 05:05:22,120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: both contain hazardous electronic waste, classified as...

4217
05:05:22,140 --> 05:05:28,040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: A-1181, and e-waste, requiring special consideration or Code 949.

4218
05:05:28,760 --> 05:05:34,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: These are Basel waste listings, illegal to be imported into the Philippines from the U.S.

4219
05:05:35,320 --> 05:05:38,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: due to the fact, again, that the U.S. is a non-party to the Convention.

4220
05:05:38,740 --> 05:05:50,580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor, what is the explanation behind the assertion that there is following of international treaty,

4221
05:05:51,020 --> 05:05:51,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: given the...

4222
05:05:52,140 --> 05:05:55,140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the citation of this representation right now?

4223
05:05:57,560 --> 05:05:59,600
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

4224
05:05:59,600 --> 05:06:05,800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the SBMA is willing to cooperate and to also submit to our Distinguished Colleague,

4225
05:06:06,160 --> 05:06:14,100
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: supporting documents that say that these materials are not hazardous,

4226
05:06:15,180 --> 05:06:20,600
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: just to establish that it also complies with all environmental compliances,

4227
05:06:20,960 --> 05:06:22,120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: as well as international.

4228
05:06:22,140 --> 05:06:25,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, we will welcome these submissions.

4229
05:06:26,620 --> 05:06:30,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But I'd like an explanation on the floor right now.

4230
05:06:31,480 --> 05:06:37,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ano po yung basihan kung bakit nasasabi, kahit succinctly po, Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor,

4231
05:06:38,480 --> 05:06:41,500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: bakit po hindi iligal yung kalakala na ito?

4232
05:06:41,940 --> 05:06:44,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ano ang basihan kung bakit hindi po iligal ito?

4233
05:06:45,020 --> 05:06:50,960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We have heard the RTC ruling, which says nga po na separate customs territory ang SBMA.

4234
05:06:51,060 --> 05:06:51,960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But I believe...

4235
05:06:52,140 --> 05:06:53,320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor,

4236
05:06:53,380 --> 05:06:56,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that doesn't mean that they are exempted from the Basel Convention,

4237
05:06:56,940 --> 05:07:00,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the DNR Department Order implementing it,

4238
05:07:00,480 --> 05:07:06,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and even other prevailing international laws and domestic regulations.

4239
05:07:06,640 --> 05:07:09,500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, Madam Speaker, we will look forward to that.

4240
05:07:09,700 --> 05:07:12,360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But ano po on the floor, succinctly, ang rason?

4241
05:07:13,020 --> 05:07:16,140
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker, just for the record also,

4242
05:07:16,680 --> 05:07:20,740
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it's because the materials are not hazardous waste.

4243
05:07:20,740 --> 05:07:21,740
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, if I may...

4244
05:07:22,140 --> 05:07:23,620
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Again, repeat.

4245
05:07:24,340 --> 05:07:29,920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: These importations are scrap mixed metals, computer accessories,

4246
05:07:30,780 --> 05:07:35,440
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: used meters, used electronics, and scrap copper, which are not hazardous.

4247
05:07:36,140 --> 05:07:41,920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, SBMA reiterates that these are not hazardous waste.

4248
05:07:42,080 --> 05:07:47,520
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And so, the importation of such materials are not violated,

4249
05:07:47,520 --> 05:07:51,460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: or doesn't violate international treaties and the Basel Convention as well.

4250
05:07:52,140 --> 05:08:01,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Under what legal basis can the SBMA provide now to say that they are not hazardous waste?

4251
05:08:01,080 --> 05:08:03,360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is this internal assessment?

4252
05:08:03,760 --> 05:08:13,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is this a different citation which they can state where it is classified differently

4253
05:08:13,980 --> 05:08:22,120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: because the prevailing rules as of now lists the containers as hazardous electronic wastes and e-waste,

4254
05:08:22,140 --> 05:08:23,780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: is requiring special consideration?

4255
05:08:32,180 --> 05:08:43,440
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, as for the SBMA, these materials are all inspected from importation.

4256
05:08:44,160 --> 05:08:46,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Inspected by whom, Madam Speaker? Good sponsor.

4257
05:08:46,940 --> 05:08:47,500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sorry.

4258
05:08:47,780 --> 05:08:48,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Inspected by whom?

4259
05:08:49,540 --> 05:08:50,920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: By the SBMA, Madam Speaker.

4260
05:08:51,260 --> 05:08:51,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is the...

4261
05:08:51,980 --> 05:08:55,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: The Bureau of Customs and DNR involved in the inspections, Madam Speaker. Good sponsor.

4262
05:08:56,360 --> 05:08:57,060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

4263
05:08:57,740 --> 05:08:58,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

4264
05:08:58,840 --> 05:09:10,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: For now, there is no legal basis that has been cited other than the assurance that SBMA inspected them.

4265
05:09:10,820 --> 05:09:14,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, given the limited time that I have,

4266
05:09:15,200 --> 05:09:21,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: let it be stated on the record that to the question and to the...

4267
05:09:21,980 --> 05:09:26,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: legal basis that this representation cited, there has been no counter-legal basis provided.

4268
05:09:27,000 --> 05:09:35,700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, my next line of question would be regarding the position of SBMA

4269
05:09:35,700 --> 05:09:44,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: in relation to a Committee on Ecology meeting I had the opportunity to attend on March 11, 2026,

4270
05:09:44,840 --> 05:09:51,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: where our topic is hazardous waste management and strengthening the Environmental Management Bureau.

4271
05:09:51,380 --> 05:10:01,420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We talked about the possible amendment of the Toxic and Hazardous Wastes Act present and prevailing in our jurisprudence now.

4272
05:10:02,140 --> 05:10:12,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: SBMA was in attendance and it gave the position that they are pushing for the designation of free trade zones such as SUBIC

4273
05:10:12,180 --> 05:10:15,600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to become Basel Convention Free Zones.

4274
05:10:16,640 --> 05:10:21,220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, ano pong ibig sabihin ng SBMA nung sinabi niya na gustong maging Basel Convention Free Zone

4275
05:10:22,660 --> 05:10:24,060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ang Subic Freeport?

4276
05:10:25,900 --> 05:10:32,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And is the agency asking for an exception from international treaties and our local environmental laws?

4277
05:10:43,140 --> 05:10:51,360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, the reason cited by the SBMA is some locators would want to

4278
05:10:51,400 --> 05:11:06,900
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: expand their operations to include imports from the United States, and because the United States is not a signatory of the Basel Convention, that is the basis for the statement of the SBMA.

4279
05:11:06,900 --> 05:11:51,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, I think desiring trade with the United States is not a heavy enough justification to look for an exception from a prevailing international treaty that seeks to protect the Philippines from the transboundary waste trade disproportionately affecting Southeast Asian countries, to the point that there has to be a call from Southeast Asian countries that [unclear] not the

4280
05:11:51,300 --> 05:12:21,800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: dumping ground or trash can of developed countries. But at the end of the day, it will remove us from protections already in place, not just in discussion with the US but also with other countries that may seek to do trade.

4281
05:12:21,800 --> 05:12:30,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, we will ask instead for a written explanation for that comment given in the March 11, 2026 hearing.

4282
05:12:30,700 --> 05:12:38,000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My next question, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, magkano po ba ang kinikita ng SBMA mula sa kalakalan ng recyclable waste?

4283
05:12:41,060 --> 05:12:45,120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: How much, I assume, of course, may kita ang ating mga locators dyan.

4284
05:12:45,400 --> 05:12:48,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: How much of it goes to SBMA, Madam Speaker, good sponsor?

4285
05:13:19,300 --> 05:13:42,320
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: [unclear] If the distinguished colleague will be willing to allow our distinguished sponsor and the SBMA family to submit a written report.

4286
05:13:50,700 --> 05:14:04,200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Okay, for payments of recyclers, as per SBMA data, it's around 200, sorry, 205 million pesos, Madam Speaker.

4287
05:14:05,300 --> 05:14:10,540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 205,864,939 pesos for 2025.

4288
05:14:12,780 --> 05:14:20,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, in the interest of time, we will also be requesting the same to be submitted via a written report.

4289
05:14:21,320 --> 05:14:32,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: As well as details on how much private recycling facilities yield in profit, alongside how much that would go to SBMA.

4290
05:14:32,700 --> 05:14:35,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My next question would be in relation to its budget.

4291
05:14:36,260 --> 05:14:45,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: SBMA's proposed 500 million subsidy is for ecozone infrastructure, but the NEP also records 1 billion in unreleased 2025 appropriations.

4292
05:14:46,560 --> 05:14:50,040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Has that amount now been released, Madam Speaker? We'd like to seek a clarification.

4293
05:14:50,040 --> 05:14:53,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Which brought, maybe that, Madam Speaker?

4294
05:15:00,000 --> 05:15:07,500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It hasn't been released yet, Madam Speaker.

4295
05:15:07,840 --> 05:15:10,460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: It has not yet been released, Madam Speaker.

4296
05:15:10,660 --> 05:15:18,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We also just ask to submit by report which projects are affected because of its non-release yet

4297
05:15:18,820 --> 05:15:24,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and what must be resolved before they can proceed, Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor.

4298
05:15:24,280 --> 05:15:25,380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: As we will comply, Madam Speaker.

4299
05:15:25,380 --> 05:15:32,400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My next question would be in relation to the joint efforts of the BOC, the DENREMB, and SBMA,

4300
05:15:32,900 --> 05:15:34,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: as stated and referenced earlier.

4301
05:15:35,080 --> 05:15:39,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We saw that in July 1 of this year, they publicly posted that they conducted a joint inspection

4302
05:15:39,940 --> 05:15:42,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: on several recycling locators in Subic.

4303
05:15:43,100 --> 05:15:47,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Can this representation be furnished with a copy of this report, Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor?

4304
05:15:48,140 --> 05:15:49,380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, we will comply, Madam Speaker.

4305
05:15:50,980 --> 05:15:54,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor, if ma, masama po sana,

4306
05:15:54,640 --> 05:15:54,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ilan ang...

4307
05:15:55,380 --> 05:15:59,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: di lang ng mga nag-ooperate ng mga recycling locators doon

4308
05:15:59,840 --> 05:16:07,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: because when we asked DENREMB yesterday, wala raw po silang data on the recycling facilities in Subic.

4309
05:16:07,540 --> 05:16:13,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And so, the appropriate agency to ask would be the one...

4310
05:16:13,860 --> 05:16:15,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: SBMA, Madam Speaker, Good Sponsor.

4311
05:16:15,800 --> 05:16:16,580
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

4312
05:16:16,860 --> 05:16:23,120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: We'll also give our distinguished colleague a copy, but there are, as of now, 14 active locators, 18 total.

4313
05:16:23,320 --> 05:16:24,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: 14, 1-4?

4314
05:16:24,420 --> 05:16:25,140
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 1-4, yes.

4315
05:16:25,380 --> 05:16:25,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: 14, Madam Speaker.

4316
05:16:25,960 --> 05:16:27,700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: We will submit the list, Madam Speaker.

4317
05:16:27,900 --> 05:16:28,320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you.

4318
05:16:28,560 --> 05:16:36,420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And my last line of questioning, Madam Speaker, this would be in relation to the public pronouncements of SBMA

4319
05:16:36,420 --> 05:16:37,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: in relation to Paxilica.

4320
05:16:37,980 --> 05:16:48,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We have seen that sa pinirmahan na MOU ng SBMA at BCDA, may pagbubukas na gagamitin ng Subic Bayport

4321
05:16:48,520 --> 05:16:52,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: bilang quote-unquote maritime gateway ng Paxilica.

4322
05:16:52,380 --> 05:16:54,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Maari po bang malaman ang extent nito?

4323
05:17:03,930 --> 05:17:09,000
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: I believe that was the last question of our distinguished colleague.

4324
05:17:10,400 --> 05:17:17,600
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: And after the sponsor response, may we request our distinguished colleague from Kabataan Party List to wrap up.

4325
05:17:17,720 --> 05:17:19,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yes, Madam Speaker, it will be my last question.

4326
05:17:19,840 --> 05:17:24,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I just like to note that according to the press release, the port will serve DAO.

4327
05:17:25,380 --> 05:17:29,400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: It's a critical gateway enabling the efficient movement of raw materials into the country

4328
05:17:29,400 --> 05:17:32,280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and timely delivery of finished products to customers.

4329
05:17:32,460 --> 05:17:35,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So we'd like clarification sa extent nito, Madam Speaker.

4330
05:17:35,480 --> 05:17:35,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Good sponsor.

4331
05:17:36,400 --> 05:17:37,200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

4332
05:17:37,680 --> 05:17:39,540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: This is a non-binding agreement.

4333
05:17:39,880 --> 05:17:42,200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: It's a MOU between BCDA and SBMA.

4334
05:17:43,400 --> 05:17:53,200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So it's just restricted to the use of Port of Subic, the limited use of Port of Subic for the maritime logistics requirements of the proposed project.

4335
05:17:54,260 --> 05:17:55,360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay, a copy of this MOU.

4336
05:17:55,380 --> 05:17:57,540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: A copy of this MOU would also be requested, Madam Speaker.

4337
05:17:57,640 --> 05:17:58,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Good sponsor.

4338
05:17:58,120 --> 05:17:59,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I have no further questions.

4339
05:17:59,280 --> 05:18:00,800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you for your time and for the clarification.

4340
05:18:01,020 --> 05:18:01,640
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

4341
05:18:02,280 --> 05:18:02,560
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ...

4342
05:18:04,500 --> 05:18:08,600
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Antonio Tino for his interpellation.

4343
05:18:08,720 --> 05:18:10,400
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Antonio Tino is recognized.

4344
05:18:25,380 --> 05:18:28,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

4345
05:18:29,260 --> 05:18:34,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilang mga tanong po sa sponsor natin.

4346
05:18:35,860 --> 05:18:42,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, I'll ask the sponsor to explain.

4347
05:18:43,060 --> 05:18:50,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ba ang ambag ng SBMA sa ekonomiya ng Pilipinas?

4348
05:18:50,960 --> 05:18:51,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mahalaga ba?

4349
05:18:52,600 --> 05:18:53,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Malaki ba?

4350
05:18:54,260 --> 05:18:54,820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Malaki.

4351
05:18:55,380 --> 05:19:02,600
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, briefly, as of now, there are 1,783 locators.

4352
05:19:02,600 --> 05:19:09,260
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Ang ini-employ po ang may trabaho dahil sa SBMA ay 174,930 na tao.

4353
05:19:10,280 --> 05:19:16,100
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Ang total investment na nakuha na ng SBMA ay 610 billion pesos.

4354
05:19:18,600 --> 05:19:24,980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Tapos ang nabigay na sa Pambansang Pamalaan through dividends is 12.15.

4355
05:19:25,380 --> 05:19:27,760
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 12.15 billion pesos, Madam Speaker.

4356
05:19:28,820 --> 05:19:31,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, 12.15 billion pesos ang nabigay.

4357
05:19:31,580 --> 05:19:34,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Iyan po ba para sa isang taon?

4358
05:19:34,320 --> 05:19:35,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Which year was that?

4359
05:19:35,620 --> 05:19:36,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Could you just clarify?

4360
05:19:36,980 --> 05:19:38,540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mula 1999, Madam Speaker.

4361
05:19:38,560 --> 05:19:39,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mula 1999.

4362
05:19:40,280 --> 05:19:40,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4363
05:19:40,520 --> 05:19:46,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, okay, 174,000 plus ang employed.

4364
05:19:47,020 --> 05:19:49,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And you mentioned over 1,000 locators.

4365
05:19:49,460 --> 05:19:50,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilan po yung locators?

4366
05:19:50,620 --> 05:19:52,360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 1,783.

4367
05:19:52,760 --> 05:19:53,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: As of June.

4368
05:19:53,560 --> 05:19:54,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 1,783 locators.

4369
05:19:55,380 --> 05:19:58,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ibig sabihin, iba't-ibang mga negosyo.

4370
05:19:59,180 --> 05:20:00,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mga foreign investor po ba ito?

4371
05:20:01,840 --> 05:20:02,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O hindi lahat?

4372
05:20:03,360 --> 05:20:04,860
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Foreign and domestic po, mix po.

4373
05:20:04,980 --> 05:20:07,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Foreign and domestic investors.

4374
05:20:08,760 --> 05:20:10,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And in terms of...

4375
05:20:12,980 --> 05:20:15,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba? May mga information din tayo rito.

4376
05:20:15,500 --> 05:20:16,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: How big is the zone?

4377
05:20:16,780 --> 05:20:17,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is it...

4378
05:20:17,540 --> 05:20:18,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: How big is the zone?

4379
05:20:21,680 --> 05:20:23,900
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 60,000 square kilometers, Madam Speaker.

4380
05:20:23,900 --> 05:20:24,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Square?

4381
05:20:25,380 --> 05:20:29,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sixty-seven square, siguro, hektars po.

4382
05:20:29,680 --> 05:20:32,680
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Sixty thousand square meters.

4383
05:20:32,680 --> 05:20:33,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano ilan yun yung hektars?

4384
05:20:33,940 --> 05:20:34,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hektars siguro.

4385
05:20:34,980 --> 05:20:36,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hektars.

4386
05:20:36,080 --> 05:20:37,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi naman po square kilometers.

4387
05:20:37,680 --> 05:20:39,680
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Sixty-seven thousand hektars.

4388
05:20:39,680 --> 05:20:41,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sixty-seven thousand hektars.

4389
05:20:41,880 --> 05:20:47,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And is it correct there are 15 operational piers and wharves?

4390
05:20:48,060 --> 05:20:51,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kasi subik harbor yan, di ba?

4391
05:20:52,260 --> 05:20:54,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, mainly port, it used to be.

4392
05:20:54,700 --> 05:20:55,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam naman natin.

4393
05:20:55,220 --> 05:20:56,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: A naval base, di ba?

4394
05:20:57,180 --> 05:20:57,400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

4395
05:20:57,440 --> 05:20:58,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, is that correct?

4396
05:20:58,300 --> 05:21:01,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: There are 15 operational piers and wharves?

4397
05:21:01,760 --> 05:21:03,120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker, we confirm.

4398
05:21:03,460 --> 05:21:03,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4399
05:21:05,500 --> 05:21:06,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Container throughput.

4400
05:21:06,760 --> 05:21:08,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ito, may mga info po tayong nakuha.

4401
05:21:08,420 --> 05:21:10,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung container, shipping container.

4402
05:21:11,500 --> 05:21:14,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi po rito, latest figure 2024.

4403
05:21:15,500 --> 05:21:17,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Roughly 600,000 TEU.

4404
05:21:19,500 --> 05:21:24,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, parang container, yun yung standard measure ng container size, di ba?

4405
05:21:25,220 --> 05:21:25,980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

4406
05:21:25,980 --> 05:21:27,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is that more or less correct?

4407
05:21:28,220 --> 05:21:30,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ganon, yung shipping na dumadaan dyan?

4408
05:21:31,160 --> 05:21:33,780
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, total capacity is 600,000, Madam Speaker.

4409
05:21:34,100 --> 05:21:34,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4410
05:21:35,600 --> 05:21:44,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At in terms of GDP, meron ba kayong figure sa ambag ng subik sa GDP, kumbaga, ng Pilipinas?

4411
05:21:50,980 --> 05:21:55,200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Meron lang po tayo for, ano, well, overall contribution to the national economy.

4412
05:21:55,220 --> 05:22:12,300
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, for 2020, isa sabi dito po yung collections from the Bureau of Customs, yung mga taxes po na binabayaran sa BIR, yung dividends po na babayaran sa national government, tapos sa LGU share.

4413
05:22:12,860 --> 05:22:18,180
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, 2025 po, 53.1 billion pesos.

4414
05:22:19,120 --> 05:22:24,440
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Consistent po na over 50 billion since 2022, per year, na nabibigay po ng SBMA.

4415
05:22:24,440 --> 05:22:25,200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Consistent po na.

4416
05:22:25,220 --> 05:22:28,700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Over 50 billion po ang naibibigay ng SBMA.

4417
05:22:28,700 --> 05:22:33,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Consistently, over 50 billion ang nabibigay ng subik ng SBMA. Tama po ba?

4418
05:22:34,100 --> 05:22:34,360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Apo.

4419
05:22:34,480 --> 05:22:44,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa national government. So, safe to say, napakahalaga po nito, hindi lang sa regional economy ng Region 3, kundi national economy. Tama po ba?

4420
05:22:44,800 --> 05:22:45,560
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Apo, Madam Speaker.

4421
05:22:45,600 --> 05:22:46,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama. Okay.

4422
05:22:47,260 --> 05:22:50,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At kanina, pinanong natin sa BCDA,

4423
05:22:53,180 --> 05:22:53,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kinonfirm nila.

4424
05:22:53,960 --> 05:23:08,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Gusto ko rin marinig sa inyo, nagkaroon po ng MOU sa pagitan ng BCDA at SBMA designating the port of subik as the primary entry and exit point for logistics, etc. under Paxilica. Correct?

4425
05:23:09,420 --> 05:23:10,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba yun?

4426
05:23:10,280 --> 05:23:10,940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

4427
05:23:11,320 --> 05:23:17,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, in other words, involved din po sa Paxilica ang subik. Tama po?

4428
05:23:18,920 --> 05:23:21,020
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker. As a port.

4429
05:23:21,260 --> 05:23:23,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: As the port. Parang dito yung main na...

4430
05:23:23,960 --> 05:23:33,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Entry and exit point. Dalu yan ng mga investment, produkto, and so on. Including, for example, energy. Parang ganun po yung narinig natin.

4431
05:23:35,420 --> 05:23:45,460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, as per the MOU, binasignate lang po ang port of subik as yung gateway for the maritime logistics requirements.

4432
05:23:45,460 --> 05:23:53,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Sige. Okay. Now, yung subik, hindi po yan EDCA site, hindi po ba?

4433
05:23:53,960 --> 05:23:55,340
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Hindi po, Madam Speaker.

4434
05:23:57,340 --> 05:24:11,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And necessarily, hindi siya EDCA site kasi yung mga approved locations under the EDCA agreement, they have to be properties provided by the AFP and DND, mga military locations. So, subik, hindi. Tama?

4435
05:24:12,100 --> 05:24:12,740
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Hindi po, Madam Speaker.

4436
05:24:12,740 --> 05:24:21,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nevertheless, tama rin po ba na malaganap ang gamit ng US military sa subik? Is that correct?

4437
05:24:23,960 --> 05:24:25,960
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

4438
05:24:25,960 --> 05:24:27,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4439
05:24:39,960 --> 05:24:43,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Naku, yung oras tumutuloy, Madam Speaker. So, i-consider nyo na lang yan.

4440
05:24:43,200 --> 05:24:53,560
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: If our distinguished colleague is amenable, the SBMA family can actually furnish your office to our good sponsor, a written response to your queries.

4441
05:24:53,960 --> 05:25:00,060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. That would be great, Madam Speaker. But I think the sponsor is also ready to give a response.

4442
05:25:00,820 --> 05:25:10,080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes. The SBMA confirms that there are economic activities that involve American firms, American actors.

4443
05:25:10,400 --> 05:25:13,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: American firms servicing the US military. Correct?

4444
05:25:14,620 --> 05:25:15,740
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes. Yes, Madam Speaker.

4445
05:25:15,740 --> 05:25:23,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For example, let me cite, ito based on mga open source research, diba? Subik Dry Dock Corporation. Tama po ba?

4446
05:25:23,960 --> 05:25:24,960
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

4447
05:25:24,960 --> 05:25:31,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ginagawa nila, repair and overhaul of US Navy vessels. Correct?

4448
05:25:32,560 --> 05:25:33,360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

4449
05:25:33,660 --> 05:25:48,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. The PCSPC fuel terminal, yung pinakamalaking fuel depot sa buong bansa, in fact, that is owned by an American equity firm, I-squared Capital.

4450
05:25:48,220 --> 05:25:49,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

4451
05:25:49,420 --> 05:25:53,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At, hindi po ba, among others, it stores fuel...

4452
05:25:53,960 --> 05:26:06,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It stores fuel for exclusive use of the US Navy. Tama po ba? Among others, hindi lahat. Hindi lahat. Pero merong fuel na ginagamit ng US Navy.

4453
05:26:06,460 --> 05:26:07,840
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Non-exclusive, Madam Speaker.

4454
05:26:07,840 --> 05:26:11,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Not exclusive. Pero meron. Tama po. Correct?

4455
05:26:11,520 --> 05:26:12,020
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

4456
05:26:12,020 --> 05:26:19,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Alam ko, yung recently, yung PNOC, bumili ng diesel, tapos nilagay din dyan. Tama po ba?

4457
05:26:19,460 --> 05:26:20,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Correct.

4458
05:26:23,960 --> 05:26:33,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Strategic Oil Reserve or Fuel Reserve ay nandyan, katabi nung fuel ng US Navy. Tama po?

4459
05:26:34,560 --> 05:26:34,760
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Opo.

4460
05:26:34,760 --> 05:26:35,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama. Okay.

4461
05:26:37,380 --> 05:26:53,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: February 2025, US Marine Corps Repositioning Warehouse. This is a 5,300 square meter facility used to store vehicle communications assets, engineering assets. Correct?

4462
05:26:53,960 --> 05:26:56,300
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, we confirm, Madam Speaker.

4463
05:26:56,300 --> 05:27:01,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Correct. So yung US Marine Corps, meron silang storage facility dyan.

4464
05:27:04,020 --> 05:27:11,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Army staging. Aguila, Subic. Processing and storage of US Army equipment.

4465
05:27:13,380 --> 05:27:23,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba? Ito, yung Aguila facility sa Subic, ginagamit ng US Army naman ito.

4466
05:27:23,960 --> 05:27:25,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Isa, Marine Corps. Ito naman, Army.

4467
05:27:27,440 --> 05:27:36,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And the contractor for that is an American logistics contractor for the U.S. military known as V2X.

4468
05:27:38,300 --> 05:27:42,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun po, V2X. Alam po niyan ni Chairman.

4469
05:27:42,700 --> 05:27:48,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. V2X is a defense contractor for logistics ng U.S. military.

4470
05:27:49,360 --> 05:27:50,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So ginagamit nila yan.

4471
05:27:50,500 --> 05:28:05,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun, part of Subic Bay, ginagamit routinely for maintenance ng mga U.S. Navy ships including submarines.

4472
05:28:07,080 --> 05:28:12,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba, yung mga Ohio-class nuclear submarines ng U.S. ay nandyan.

4473
05:28:13,480 --> 05:28:18,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dumadaong dyan, nagpapaayos, nagpaparefuel, and so on and so forth.

4474
05:28:18,600 --> 05:28:36,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The most recent incident being a U.S. destroyer that was recently stranded for four days in the South China Sea.

4475
05:28:37,300 --> 05:28:42,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tapos nawala ng kuryente. Tapos dinala sa Subic. Tama po ba?

4476
05:28:45,580 --> 05:28:47,220
